{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>Of the most holy sacrifices and of the sacrifices.</b> If it says 'of the most holy sacrifices,' why does it say 'and of the sacrifices he shall eat'? Rather, had it said 'of the most holy sacrifices' and not said 'and of the sacrifices he shall eat,' I would have said: most holy sacrifices that are permitted to a non-priest — he may eat of them, but ordinary sacrifices he may not eat. Therefore it says 'and of the sacrifices he shall eat.' And had it said 'and of the sacrifices he shall eat' and not said 'of the most holy sacrifices,' I would have said: of the sacrifices he may eat, but of the most holy sacrifices he may not eat. Therefore it is necessary to say both 'of the most holy sacrifices' and 'and of the sacrifices.'"], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:14:11.525352207Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}